      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ?$",
      "worked_solution": "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(0,a).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|4|=4$ centered at the point $(0,4),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/3b15873d4cd95216db84ecccbad4394397469c501745663605c3ac360c2d723e.png)",
